{
 "schemaVersion": 1,
 "name": "gridfinity-thin-plate",
 "description": "Build the Gridfinity 2x2 baseplate as a feature tree of THIN custom features that mirror the native modelling steps (variable, sketch, extrude): a head of `Thin Variable` rows names every number the profile repeats, then one rounded body sketch, the 45 deg socket profile as four stacked subtraction layers (clearance, ramp, lock face, flare) and the magnet pockets as a shaft plus a 45 deg mouth chamfer. Repeated numbers are cited as `#variable` rather than retyped, so a human changes the cell pitch in ONE row and the whole plate follows; the one-off numbers (layer heights, a layer's own depth) stay literal. Every row carries its numbers in the ONE transaction that creates it, so no row is ever added with defaults and edited afterwards. After the run, success is verified outside the runner with browser_get_partstudio_features, a STEP export and a B-rep face inventory (the mesh report cannot tell an R4 corner from a sharp one). This project deliberately contains NO source-refresh step: committing dev/fixtures-capture/thin-native-features.fs is the separate project thin-features-refresh-fs, because browser_deploy_and_apply_featurescript reports success only as built=true, which requires the apply to leave at least one COMPUTED PART, and a sketch-only row creates a sketch with no part (measured 2026-09-20). Every step below therefore only inserts rows. Every step that fills an Onshape expression also states expect_values, the value that expression must EVALUATE to, because a settled quantity widget renders the resolved number rather than the typed `#variable` and the typed text is only the pre-parse state -- an accept taken on it commits the field's previous value (measured live 2026-09-21). A variable's `description` is a string VALUE, so it carries the Chinese text: only annotations are restricted to printable ASCII, and a non-ASCII annotation kills the whole feature (onshape_docs/experience/featurescript.md).",
 "steps": [
  {
   "id": "00-var-pitch",
   "tool": "browser_insert_custom_feature",
   "args": {
    "feature_name": "Thin Variable",
    "part_studio_tab": "GF Thin Plate",
    "parameters": {
     "name": "gf_pitch",
     "value": "42 mm",
     "description": "格距：相邻格子中心距"
    },
    "confirm_mutation": true
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "01-var-plate-size",
   "tool": "browser_insert_custom_feature",
   "args": {
    "feature_name": "Thin Variable",
    "part_studio_tab": "GF Thin Plate",
    "parameters": {
     "name": "gf_plate_size",
     "value": "#gf_pitch * 2",
     "description": "2×2 底板外形尺寸"
    },
    "expect_row": "#gf_plate_size = 84 mm",
    "expect_values": {
     "value": "84 mm"
    },
    "confirm_mutation": true
   }
  },
  {
